PRACTICAL – 7
Title:

Performing Android Application Vulnerability Assessment using QARK

Aim:

To perform vulnerability assessment of an Android application using QARK.

Objectives:
To understand Android application vulnerability assessment
To install and configure QARK on Linux
To analyze APK files using QARK
To identify security vulnerabilities and insecure coding practices
To generate vulnerability assessment reports
Procedure:
(i) Install Required Packages

Open terminal and run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3 python3-pip git -y
(ii) Download QARK

Clone QARK repository:

git clone https://github.com/linkedin/qark.git

Navigate into directory:

cd qark
(iii) Install QARK
pip install . --break-system-packages

Verify installation:

qark --help
(iv) Obtain APK File

Place APK file (DivaApplication.apk) in working directory.

(v) Run QARK Analysis

Analyze APK:

qark --apk DivaApplication.apk
(vi) Review Analysis Results

QARK checks for:

Insecure permissions
Exported components
Weak cryptography
Hardcoded secrets
Insecure intents
Vulnerable activities and services
(vii) Generate Vulnerability Report

Observe generated:

HTML report
Vulnerability summary
Risk levels and recommendations
Observation:
QARK successfully analyzed the Android APK
Security vulnerabilities and insecure coding practices were identified
Exported activities and insecure permissions were detected
Vulnerability reports with recommendations were generated
Result:

Android application vulnerability assessment was successfully performed using QARK. The tool identified insecure configurations, vulnerable components, and potential security risks within the application.

Viva Questions:
Q: What is QARK?

👉 Quick Android Review Kit used for Android application security assessment.

Q: What does QARK detect?

👉 Insecure permissions, exported components, weak cryptography, and coding vulnerabilities.

Q: Why is vulnerability assessment important?

👉 To identify and fix security weaknesses before deployment.

Q: What type of analysis does QARK perform?

👉 Static security analysis of Android applications.

